Title: England vs India: Brydon Carse keeps England alive on fourth day at Lord's
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'England batting coach Marcus Trescothick', 'Text': "We would have loved 250 and beyond but we would have taken 190 and our chance to bowl on that pitch and it'll come down to who holds the pressure best.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 34, 'StartChar': 48, 'EndChar': 188}}, {'Speaker': 'India all-rounder Washington Sundar', 'Text': "We'd have loved to have about nine wickets [in hand]. It is what it is and we'll definitely win the game.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 36, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 116}}, {'Speaker': 'India all-rounder Washington Sundar', 'Text': "We'd have loved to have about nine wickets [in hand]. It is what it is and we'll definitely win the game.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 38, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 116}}, {'Speaker': 'Washington Sundar', 'Text': "All four of them, honestly. Lord's Test, big Test, it's going to be amazing when we win the game and go 2-1 up in the series so every wicket was very very crucial.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 40, 'StartChar': 48, 'EndChar': 197}}, {'Speaker': 'Washington Sundar', 'Text': "All four of them, honestly. Lord's Test, big Test, it's going to be amazing when we win the game and go 2-1 up in the series so every wicket was very very crucial.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 42, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 149}}, {'Speaker': 'BBC chief cricket commentator Jonathan Agnew', 'Text': "We're all a bit hoarse after that. It was absolutely gripping. Even World Cup finals don't quite generate that kind of madness.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 44, 'StartChar': 56, 'EndChar': 195}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'Bowling with supreme rhythm from the Pavilion End, Carse pinned both Karun Nair and India captain Shubman Gill leg before.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 96}}, {'Description': 'With the final ball of the day, Ben Stokes bowled nightwatchman Akash Deep to leave India 58-4, 135 adrift of their target of 193.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 114}}, {'Description': 'In a chaotic morning, Harry Brook was bowled trying to sweep seamer Akash Deep for 23. Joe Root dropped anchor for 40, Stokes even more guarded for 33.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 122}}, {'Description': 'Both the captain past and present were bowled by Sundar, part of a total of 12 home batters that have lost their furniture - an England record for a Test in this country.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 138}}, {'Description': 'Jofra Archer bounced out Yashasvi Jaiswal for nought, but Chris Woakes could not cling on to a return catch off KL Rahul when he had only five.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 121}}, {'Description': "England were drifting out of the game until Carse's intervention, before the talismanic Stokes had the final say. It will be a grandstand finale on Monday morning.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 132}}, {'Description': 'Off-spinner Shoaib Bashir, who damaged his finger on day three, is available to bowl for England if required, though looks set to be ruled out of the final two Tests.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 135}}, {'Description': "Finally, after three torpid days, this Test exploded into life. The pitch became a snake pit, there was tension between the teams after the Saturday evening handbags and the Lord's atmosphere was sizzling.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 189}}, {'Description': 'From the second over of the day, when Bumrah got one to spit at Zak Crawley off a length, the action was never anything less than riveting.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 12, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 116}}, {'Description': "India's bowlers were outstanding, the seamers in the morning and Sundar across the afternoon. England's approach can be questioned, especially Brook's dismissal, but the fact a maestro like Root had to face 96 balls for his 40 runs, with only one four, shows how difficult batting was.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 13, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 228}}, {'Description': 'Bumrah was mesmeric. As he stalked in during the evening, the large number of India fans chanted his name, a foreboding din. It was equally as loud when Archer removed Jaiswal.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 155}}, {'Description': 'It was the India fans enjoying the evening sun until Carse charged down the slope. Nair misjudged to play no shot and Gill, who had already overturned being given caught behind, was undone by a nip-backer.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 177}}, {'Description': "England's fielders revved up the crowd, Akash Deep appeared as nightwatchman and wasted as much time as possible, but not enough. What theatre.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 16, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 116}}, {'Description': 'England owe much to Carse after their batting buckled. No doubt run-scoring was tough, though the home side did not help themselves with their decision making.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 18, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 129}}, {'Description': 'Whether it was the toughness of the conditions, or the feeling between the teams, England got carried away in the morning session. Ben Duckett played a needless swipe and Crawley, who bravely fended off Bumrah, fell with a familiar loose drive.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 19, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 190}}, {'Description': 'At what point does his untouchable place at the top of the order come into question?', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 20, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 71}}, {'Description': 'Most infuriating was Brook. Twice he ramped Deep for four, then hit the same bowler for a straight six. Next over, Deep moved a fielder fine on the leg side, so Brook attempted a sweep and was bowled.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 21, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 189}}, {'Description': 'England might feel aggrieved that India used substitute keeper Dhruv Jurel, who was excellent standing up to the seamers. Still, standing back he conceded the majority of his 25 byes, without which the game might already be as good as gone.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 22, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 193}}, {'Description': 'Root threatened one of his epics to dig England out of trouble, Stokes never got to the stage where he flicked his trademark switch. The wickets fell in a cluster of four, then six, either side of their stand of 67.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 23, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 160}}, {'Description': "Archer needed only one ball at Jaiswal to bounce him out and the true cost of Woakes' drop of Rahul is still to be revealed. Carse, though, was irresistible.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 24, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 119}}], 'Image': []}
